This code aims to solve the problem in a numerically accurate way. It treats each tile as a node in a graph and each move from one tile to an adjacent tile as an edge where the weight is the difference in shading between the tiles. The code uses a priority queue to find the minimum augmentation of the graph, which in this context is the minimum possible contrast, confined to a numerical set up to prevent underflows or overflows.

